abstract: >-
  Asking a model to check its work can improve the answer and still make the
  returned response unusable. This paper defines boundary contamination as any
  non-whitespace text outside the required deliverable, scores it separately
  from deliverable correctness across three experiments, and audits the
  measuring instrument that produced the results.
